{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-11-09T08:09:07Z", "actor": "sports", "story": {"id": "st-80521c502aec", "date": "2026-11-09", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Basel blow 2-0 lead at Thun", "summary": "Basel are winless in five league games after a 3-3 draw at Thun.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/fussball/super-league/13-runde-der-super-league-spaetes-eigentor-basel-muss-sich-in-thun-mit-3-3-begnuegen", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Basel have now gone five league games without a win, and SRF reports they still sit \"below the line\" in the table, one place behind Thun, who edged past Luzern with the point. Basel led 2–0 inside 12 minutes (Zan Celar after 40 seconds, Philip Otele), then goalkeeper Jonas Omlin tried to dribble on a slick pitch and handed Thun a goal; Kevin Rüegg's late own goal (78th minute) completed the comeback. Thun are still without a home league win after six attempts. SRF refers to Basel as the reigning champions, so five games without a win is a real slump. In the same round Lugano lost 5–0 at St. Gallen, while Servette–Zürich ended goalless. The league now pauses for two weeks of international matches; Basel host Luzern on Sunday 2026-11-22.", "why": "the Basel form that stalled at 0–0 against GC on 2026-10-25 has not recovered, and the international break gives the coach two weeks to fix a defence that gave away three goals to a side that had not won at home.", "thread_id": "2026-10-26-sports-lugano-lead-basel-stall-at-0-0", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-26", "event_date": "2026-11-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["FC Basel", "FC Thun"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-11-09T08:09:07Z", "updated": "2026-11-09T08:09:07Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-11-09-sports-basel-blow-2-0-lead-at-thun"], "editions": ["2026-11-09-sports"], "origin": "writer:sports", "streams": ["sports"]}}
