{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-11-09T08:09:07Z", "actor": "sports", "story": {"id": "st-4f0bdbfb82bc", "date": "2026-11-09", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Norris wins Brazilian GP", "summary": "Norris won in the wet ahead of Verstappen as Mercedes clinched the constructors' title.", "url": "https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-brazilian-gp-lando-norris-wins-in-mixed-conditions-mercedes-clinches-constructors-title/10873048/", "source_domain": "autosport.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Lando Norris (McLaren) converted pole into his third win of 2026, holding off Max Verstappen, who finished second after starting from the back of the grid on an engine-change penalty; Isack Hadjar made it a double podium for Red Bull. Mercedes finished fourth and fifth (George Russell, new champion Kimi Antonelli) and that was enough to secure the constructors' championship, the team's ninth and first since 2021. The driver title was already decided, so the interest was in the team race and in Verstappen's recovery. Lewis Hamilton finished ninth and says tensions with Ferrari team-mate Charles Leclerc are \"squashed\".", "why": "both titles now belong to Mercedes, so the remaining races are about pride, seats and 2027 positioning rather than the championship.", "thread_id": "2026-11-09-sports-norris-wins-brazilian-gp", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-09", "event_date": "2026-11-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Lando Norris", "Mercedes", "Max Verstappen"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-11-09T08:09:07Z", "updated": "2026-11-09T08:09:07Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-11-09-sports-norris-wins-brazilian-gp"], "editions": ["2026-11-09-sports"], "origin": "writer:sports", "streams": ["sports"]}}
